{"id": "85842", "name": "דוגמאות לפונקציה אי-זוגית, זוגית ולא זו ולא זו – 3 סעיפים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 5, "penalty": 0.3333333, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Give an example of an odd function by typing an expression which represents it.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_1(x)=\\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:odd]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Give an example of an even function.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_2(x)=\\) [[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:even]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">c</span></div><p>Give an example of a function which is odd and even.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(f_3(x)=\\) [[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:oddeven]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-right:8px\">d</span></div><p>Is the answer to part c unique? (Or are there many different possibilities.)</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans4]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans4]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:unique]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Check each example against the definitions \\(f(-x)=-f(x)\\) (odd) and \\(f(-x)=f(x)\\) (even); combining the two definitions gives part c and part d.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — An odd function (part a)</b><br>A function is odd if \\(f(-x)=-f(x)\\) for all \\(x\\). An odd power changes sign together with \\(x\\), so \\(f_1(x)=x^3\\) works:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f_1(-x)=(-x)^3=-x^3=-f_1(x). \\]</p>Other examples: \\(x\\), \\(\\sin(x)\\), \\(x^5-2x\\).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — An even function (part b)</b><br>A function is even if \\(f(-x)=f(x)\\) for all \\(x\\). An even power removes the sign, so \\(f_2(x)=x^4\\) works:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f_2(-x)=(-x)^4=x^4=f_2(x). \\]</p>Other examples: \\(x^2\\), \\(\\cos(x)\\), \\(|x|\\), any constant.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — Odd and even (part c)</b><br>If \\(f\\) is both even and odd, then for every \\(x\\)<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f(x)=f(-x)=-f(x)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 2f(x)=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad f(x)=0. \\]</p>Conversely, the zero function satisfies both conditions, since \\(0=-0\\). Hence<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ f_3(x)=0. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 4 — Uniqueness (part d)</b><br>The computation in step 3 shows that every function which is both odd and even must be the zero function. So the answer to part c is unique:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\text{true} \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}, {"name": "ans4", "type": "boolean", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "even", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "sa:ans2-subst(x=-x,ans2);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "sa", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "even-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "even-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — incorrect.</b> Your answer is not an even function. Look, \\[ f(x)-f(-x)={@sa@} \\neq 0.\\]</div>"}}]}, {"name": "odd", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "sa:subst(x=-x,ans1)+ans1;", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "sa", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "odd-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "odd-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b> Your answer is not an odd function. Look, \\[ f(x)+f(-x)={@sa@} \\neq 0.\\]</div>"}}]}, {"name": "oddeven", "value": 2, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "sa1:subst(x=-x,ans3)+ans3;\n sa2:ans3-subst(x=-x,ans3);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "sa1", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0.5, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "ODD", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "oddeven-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is not an odd function. Look, \\[ f(x)+f(-x)={@sa1@} \\neq 0.\\]</div>"}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "sa2", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0.5, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "EVEN", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "oddeven-1-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is not an even function. Look, \\[ f(x)-f(-x)={@sa2@} \\neq 0.\\]</div>"}}]}, {"name": "unique", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans4", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "unique-0-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part d — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "unique-0-F ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part d — incorrect.</b></div>"}}]}], "qvnames": [], "nvariants": 1}